cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research or its code, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  precept-research: Conditional Pointwise V-usable Information at the
  Natural-Language Coordination Boundary Between LLM Agents
abstract: >-
  A standalone research project measuring conditional pointwise V-usable
  information (CPVI) at the natural-language handoff between two coordinating
  LLM agents in a degradable communication channel, with an in-repo runtime
  gate that can block low-information handoffs.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gian Prem
    family-names: Rajaram
repository-code: "https://github.com/gianpremrajaram/precept-research"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - V-usable information
  - multi-agent LLM coordination
  - runtime gating
  - information theory
